                <pb facs="0369" n="363" xml:id="pg363"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic">February 23,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that it is difficult at this distance to fully appreciate all the
                    circumstances which induce the ministers to insist upon further prosecutions,
                    and that the President, while disinclined to place Mr. Conger in an attitude of
                    opposition to his colleagues, instructs him to make clear to them the
                    President’s earnest desire for peace, the cessation of bloodshed, and the
                    resumption of normal relations.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
